        "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
        "body": "The six-section handover brings the release, rollback, monitoring, and maintenance notes together without losing the original monitoring details. The evidence summary makes a useful distinction between the local SQLite restore drill and a rollback on the live service, and between a green CI run and GitHub enforcing required checks on main. One suggestion is to list who will verify each open item and what evidence they should attach, especially for hosted rollback and off-host backups. Overall, this is a useful handover draft. I’d keep #208 open until the instructor confirms the section count and the team records the live checks and updated branch protection settings.",
